{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2126","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2126","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2126\",\"parent_revision\":\"c2fb4ef0f259c462468c3ba691123b20c6b7d6c81cd0b50adb85cee6124db506\",\"root_revision\":\"c2fb4ef0f259c462468c3ba691123b20c6b7d6c81cd0b50adb85cee6124db506\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA regression that breaks `init_skill.py` (e.g., wrong path resolution, missing example file, broken frontmatter template) only surfaces when a developer runs the script manually. A regression in `package_skill.py` only surfaces when someone tries to package a skill for distribution. A regression in `skilllint`'s error reporting (wrong error code emitted, missing detection) is invisible until users notice. The scaffolder and packager are the entry-point tools that all skill authors rely on; silent regressions block downstream work and are hard to root-cause.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Pattern observed in research/skill-generation-tools/waza.md \u2014 Waza's Makefile contains `smoke-statusline-installer` (mock HOME/PATH override), `smoke-english-coaching-installer` (idempotence), `smoke-package` (ZIP structure validation), `smoke-verify-skills` (6 validation edge cases). The mock-environment pattern catches scaffolder regressions that only surface in installation-time conditions.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **skill scaffolder and packager scripts have no end-to-end smoke tests in ci** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from research/skill-generation-tools/waza.md\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-04\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPre-commit hooks and CI run linters (`ruff`, `ty`, `markdownlint`, `auto_sync_manifests.py`) but no end-to-end smoke test exercises the skill scaffolder (`init_skill.py`) or packager (`package_skill.py`) against a tmpdir or mock-environment target. `init_skill.py` validates inputs but is never executed against a fresh directory in CI to confirm it produces the expected file tree. `package_skill.py` is never executed against a fixture skill in CI to confirm it produces a `.skill` ZIP with the expected entries. `uvx skilllint@latest check` is never run against a corpus of intentionally-broken fixtures to confirm it raises the expected error codes.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `.github/workflows/code-quality.yml` \u2014 runs linters only, no scaffolder or packager invocation.\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 same.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/init_skill.py` \u2014 never invoked in CI.\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/scripts/package_skill.py` \u2014 never invoked in CI.\\n- No `Makefile` smoke target at repo root, and no `scripts/smoke_tests.py`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5ac7c5ee06d5ccbd003bd2c085540b2a81e83ee3eab5fb4f295011fa65639c40\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCbbDA\"}"}